// Native canonical Python annotation text. One row for each annotation node, including type wrappers.
// Formatting follows Python 3.13 ast.unparse; no Python process runs in the engine.
// This relation describes annotations, not arbitrary source statements or signature hashes.
.decl annotation_text(n: node, s: symbol)
.input annotation_text

// Canonical receiver of a Call whose function is an Attribute. The key is the actual Call node.
// All call receivers in a demanded prepared file batch are formatted; this is not a per-node scalar callback.
.decl call_receiver_text(n: node, s: symbol)
.input call_receiver_text

// Canonical whole Call expression and its callee expression, keyed by the actual Call node.
// These share the same native parse with annotations and receivers. Only requested columns are formatted.
.decl call_text(n: node, s: symbol)
.input call_text
.decl call_function_text(n: node, s: symbol)
.input call_function_text

// Python repr(value) for non-string Constants within annotations, including nested literals.
// Includes bytes, integers, floats, complex literals, booleans, None and Ellipsis.
// Strings use str_const. Type wrappers retain the same lookup keys as annotation_text.
// These rows share its demanded native parse and do not scan literals outside annotations.
.decl annotation_constant_repr(n: node, s: symbol)
.input annotation_constant_repr

// Canonical definition expressions, keyed by the actual expression node.
// Class bases exclude metaclass and **keyword arguments; decorators retain calls.
// These columns share the demanded file batch and native parse above.
.decl decorator_text(n: node, s: symbol)
.input decorator_text
.decl class_base_text(n: node, s: symbol)
.input class_base_text
